 fact they can recognise Bob the Brujah doesn't help when suddenly everyone with a phone can spot Mr Obvious Supernatural. Lasombra have a horrible time with camera/refections in the modern nights, all Kindred having it would be bonkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that is why Blush of life solves it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T07:33:27-08:00","id":1286434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286430#post1286430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My response is:<br /> <br /> 1. Yeah, that's a theme of the game.<br /> <br /> 2. The game implies you don't remember stuff after and before the feeding.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of it being unbelievable....<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you want to play the game or not?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have vampire overpopulation due centuries of non-population control and It would make sense , but the moment in wich that already overpopulation can quintuply in a night becuase the embrace only cost 1 BP the setting stops being realistic due the menace of a zombie outbreak<br /> <br /> The game doesnt imply non remembering about feeding in any momen there is even Kiss Adicts becuase THEY REMEMBER and Dominate 3/1 exist for something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T07:44:25-08:00","id":1286439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286422#post1286422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game you want already exist: VtR. Please let Requiem be Requiem, and Masquerade be Masquerade. I want Gen. I want Antes. I want Cain. I don't want deux ex machina amnesia bite neither deux ex machina glitch on cameras/mirror.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting and the mechanics are a completly different stuff this is why you can still play masquerade with other rules and the general result will be better becuase masquerade is loved for his characters and sect conflic but berated for his mechanics and for a good reason (They aren\u00b4t coherent)<br /> <br /> PD:You can still have Antediluvians and Blood Potency in fact it makes more sense becuase it justifies their power boost to kaijus way better than generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T07:54:46-08:00","id":1286442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286434#post1286434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can have vampire overpopulation due centuries of non-population control and It would make sense , but the moment in wich that already overpopulation can quintuply in a night becuase the embrace only cost 1 BP the setting stops being realistic due the menace of a zombie outbreak<br /> <br /> The game doesnt imply non remembering about feeding in any momen there is even Kiss Adicts becuase THEY REMEMBER and Dominate 3/1 exist for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my novel, STRAIGHT OUTTA FANGTON, we have a broken masquerade but before that happened the vampire establishment was always trying to kill any younger vampire it could for the flimisest of reasons.<br /> <br /> This, of course, was the heart of the Anarch movement because the Elders really DID want them dead.<br /> <br /> They were all competing predators in the minds of the Old Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T07:55:05-08:00","id":1286443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286439#post1286439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The setting and the mechanics are a completly different stuff this is why you can still play masquerade with other rules and the general result will be better becuase masquerade is loved for his characters and sect conflic but berated for his mechanics and for a good reason (They aren\u00b4t coherent)<br /> <br /> PD:You can still have Antediluvians and Blood Potency in fact it makes more sense becuase it justifies their power boost to kaijus way better than generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>You literally described V5 attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T08:10:42-08:00","id":1286447,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24037_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24037\" data-vbnamecard=\"24037\">Leandro16</a> <br /> <br /> You know I really enjoy your offerings. Your posts are well-written, well thought-out, and entertaining. Many of them have ideas which can be very useful in a Vampire: the Masquerade game. When I see you have posted, I always look forward to reading it!<br /> <br /> One very teeny-tiny issue, though. They seem to share a common theme.<br /> <br /> Now, I like VtR, especially VtR2. It's a fun game. So is VtM. They are, however, separate and distinct games with separate and distinct mechanical systems which lead to two very different game settings. Oh, both have elements of the other, but both have things they do better. One is a game of close-up, personal horror in isolated cities. The other is a game of epic, world-spanning nocturnal warfare.<br /> <br /> While it is sometimes useful to port ideas back and forth between the two, at some point so many things get ported from VtR (which you clearly prefer) into VtM that it ceases to be VtM. Now, I'm not certain at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship_of_Theseus\" target=\"_blank\">what point that happens</a>, but if this is the case, wouldn't it make more sense for you to play VtR2 and port the parts of VtM you like into that system?<br /> <br /> Which parts of VtM are there which keep bringing you back to it, and that you would port into a VtR game which <i>do not have a similar mechanic in VtR</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T08:42:55-08:00","id":1286456,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11558_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11558\" data-vbnamecard=\"11558\">Nosimplehiway</a> O yeah I make a lot of references to requiem 2ED but aur contraire of what my comments may suggest I prefer VTM by Far becuase of the Setting is just the Mechanical aspect what I don\u00b4t like.<br /> <br /> VTR has without any doubt superior mechanics but the setting is kinda bland for my tastes compared to the 90s epic of masquerade , his characters that I have come to love and to be honest I don\u00b4t like Isolation as a theme becuase I have a not so hidden fetish over conspiracy theories so when I heard about &quot;world spanning nocturnal warfare&quot; I knew that VtM was what i was looking for.<br /> <br /> About what I would Change from Requiem the answer are tons of things: the Ventrue weakness of the masquerade is way better and the same happens with nosferatu weakness , I would port thaumaturgy paths as a rituals and change some mechacnic departments like combat or the ube , make all rolls contested not to mention that i would tweak blood potency making it not decrease during torpor and grow more slow to mimic generations Etc....In the end it makes more sense to me to tweak the masquerade becuase it alredy has the themes that i like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T08:53:35-08:00","id":1286463,"title":"","content":"<b>AGE:</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286422#post1286422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game you want already exist: VtR. Please let Requiem be Requiem, and Masquerade be Masquerade. I want Gen. I want Antes. I want Cain. I don't want deux ex machina amnesia bite neither deux ex machina glitch on cameras/mirror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the game he wants existed before VtR. The Los Angeles: A House Divided MUSH started development in 2000 and went online in early 2002 -- over two years earlier. (I ain't saying VtR stole our mechanics... I mean, maybe they did but I also think that there is an intuitive way to think about some of this stuff based on some assumptions implicit in the original VtM materials and, let us be *totally* honest here -- Van Richten's Guide to Vampires, an AD&amp;D supplement from 1992. So &quot;independent&quot; invention is far, far more likely.)<br /> <br /> We developed something like Blood Potency -- it's called &quot;Sanguinis.&quot; It works just like generation, but it advances (mostly) with age and diablerie. (If you've read my homebrew rules, you've seen the chart, which should look familiar but which I'm not posting here because the BBS system is being persnickety.)<br /> <br /> <b>EMBRACE MECHANIC:</b><br /> We also had a different embrace mechanic that implemented several new features:<ul><li>Embraces DID NOT automatically work; they could very easily fail. If a random neonate just grabbed someone off the street and tried to vamp them on a whim, the chances of success are only 10-15%.</li> <li>Success could be bolstered by spending permanent willpower, and higher Sanguinis increased the chance of success</li> <li>Regular embraces (which produce a Sanguinis 1 childe) cost 2WP, while &quot;True Childe&quot; embraces, which create a &quot;minus 1&quot; Sanguinis Childe cost 2 PERMANENT Willpower</li> <li>The number of recent embraces negatively affected survival chances as well.</li> </ul><br /> <b>KISS MECHANIC: </b><br /> I *REALLY* like the idea of &quot;Kiss amnesia.&quot; In fact, I like it so much that until I read Leandro's post above, I *DID NOT REALIZE* that it wasn't part of the normal mechanics of VtM (much like what CT Phipps describes). I had always figured that the &quot;ecstasy&quot; bit carried with it a certain amount of cloudiness. I think it's an excellent change/clarification to the rules.<br /> <br /> EDIT: One of the things that makes the Sabbat what they are in my homebrew WoD is that they actually came up with a much more effective (but still not 100%) form of Embrace, involving various rituals and something like the Vinculum. The ability to embrace more effectively is probably one of their greatest weapons against the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","user":"Legendre","date":". 02-10-2019, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T09:02:46-08:00","id":1286465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286434#post1286434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have vampire overpopulation due centuries of non-population control and It would make sense , but the moment in wich that already overpopulation can quintuply in a night becuase the embrace only cost 1 BP the setting stops being realistic due the menace of a zombie outbreak</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but who has the motive to do something like that? Every additional vampire is a potential masquerade risk, a rival for territory and food sources. And of course, as soon as other people get wind of a madman who is up to something like that, pretty much every faction would be willing to pull out all the stops to put an end to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286434#post1286434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game doesnt imply non remembering about feeding in any momen there is even Kiss Adicts becuase THEY REMEMBER and Dominate 3/1 exist for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood dolls can still work without every single victim remembering what happened. Some people simply know how great they felt when... something... happened and seek out the experience over and over again by going to the same places and interacting with the same people before finally putting together 2 and 2. And Dominate 3 is useful for Masquerade breaches, however they occur - most simply when discipline use gets observed or when there are witnesses to the feeding.<br /> <br /> And finally, to quote the book (page 211 f.):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It takes time to drink blood and care to do it prop-<br /> erly. The bite of a vampire can seem downright euphoric<br /> to the victim; vampire fangs produce a supernatural<br /> intoxicating effect while opening up a blood vessel. <i>As-<br /> suming the vampire takes the time to hit a vein or artery<br /> correctly and licks the wound closed afterward, the<br /> victim may only remember the encounter as a drug trip,<br /> an interlude of weird rough sex, or just a delirious fog<br /> of drunken intimacy.</i> Even a closed<br /> wound and <i>happy hallucination</i> for<br /> the victim might still leave behind<br /> an air embolism, to say nothing of<br /> long-term anemia.<br /> As a general rule, attempting<br /> to preserve the victim\u2019s life, health,<br /> or <i>blissed-out screen memory</i> (all<br /> of which of course also preserve<br /> the Masquerade) takes longer than<br /> simply ripping open an artery and<br /> slurping down the red stuff. On<br /> the other hand, a victim who fights<br /> back slows things down and endan-<br /> gers the Masquerade. A vampire can<br /> drain and kill a helpless or other-<br /> wise unresisting human in roughly<br /> five turns. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T10:00:06-08:00","id":1286477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286465#post1286465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but who has the motive to do something like that? Every additional vampire is a potential masquerade risk, a rival for territory and food sources. And of course, as soon as other people get wind of a madman who is up to something like that, pretty much every faction would be willing to pull out all the stops to put an end to them.<br /> <br /> Blood dolls can still work without every single victim remembering what happened. Some people simply know how great they felt when... something... happened and seek out the experience over and over again by going to the same places and interacting with the same people before finally putting together 2 and 2. And Dominate 3 is useful for Masquerade breaches, however they occur - most simply when discipline use gets observed or when there are witnesses to the feeding.<br /> <br /> And finally, to quote the book (page 211 f.):</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see any amnesia here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T10:10:42-08:00","id":1286480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>the<br /> victim may only <b>remember</b> the encounter as a <b>drug trip</b>,<br /> an <b>interlude of weird rough sex</b>, or just a <b>delirious fog</b><br /> of drunken intimacy.</i> Even a closed<br /> wound and <i><b>happy hallucination</b><br /> [...]</i><br /> <b><i>blissed-out screen memory</i></b> </div> </div> </div>Bolded the important parts for convenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T10:31:46-08:00","id":1286484,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3118_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3118\" data-vbnamecard=\"3118\">Cifer</a> The kiss doesnt erases memories it just brings enormous pleasure so kindred without Dominate try to pass it as them being gods of sex and try to control things with the blood bond.<br /> <br /> This would be sustainable if vampires where a weird minority but there are a tons of them 148880 vampires If we use the minimun recomended ratio of 1 vampire per each 50.000 humans and each of these vampires need at least 1 Blood Point per night assuming they are not using the gifts of the blood that of course they are.<br /> <br /> So we have 148880 vampires hunting every night and only one third of them has mind erase powers via dominate asuming the best case scenario becuase we both know that 1/50000 ratio is something that kindred don\u00b4t respect and that having dominate as in clan doesnt have to mean that you have devoloped the mind erasing aspect of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T11:02:07-08:00","id":1286493,"title":"","content":"If you change the embrace mechanics, you change the ecology, too. You can end up with smaller numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T11:07:57-08:00","id":1286495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286484#post1286484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3118_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3118\" data-vbnamecard=\"3118\">Cifer</a> This would be sustainable if vampires where a weird minority but there are a tons of them 148880 vampires If we use the minimun recomended ratio of 1 vampire per each 50.000</div> </div> </div> </div>The ratio is one vampire per 100,000 if I remember correctly which comes out as around 7,000 vampires. One per 50,000 would still only be around 14,000. Think you missed a zero somewhere. Imo both these numbers are relatively realistic when we're talking about the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24285-mithras","name":"Mithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T11:15:01-08:00","id":1286497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286484#post1286484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3118_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3118\" data-vbnamecard=\"3118\">Cifer</a> The kiss doesnt erases memories it just brings enormous pleasure so kindred without Dominate try to pass it as them being gods of sex and try to control things with the blood bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shall I reiterate the quote a third time? Because I can do that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>only <b>remember</b> the encounter as a <b>drug trip</b>, [...]<b> interlude of weird rough sex</b>, [...] <b>delirious fog</b> </i><i><b>happy hallucination</b> [...] </i><b><i>blissed-out screen memory</i></b> </div> </div> </div>I mean, how much clearer does the text need to be to describe that regular feeding massively interferes with the mental state of the victim up to the point where their subconscious tries to fill in the blanks with stuff that makes more sense to a modern human than &quot;I was attacked by a vampire&quot;?<br /> And no, the blood bond makes no appearance here.<br /> <br /> The far greater problem is the age-old conspiracy with thousands of members anyway, <a href=\"https://phys.org/news/2016-01-equation-large-scale-conspiracies-quickly-reveal.html\" target=\"_blank\">when smaller modern conspiracies have unraveled after a few decades at most</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","user":"Cifer","date":". 02-10-2019, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T12:48:12-08:00","id":1286511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286497#post1286497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shall I reiterate the quote a third time? Because I can do that.<br /> I mean, how much clearer does the text need to be to describe that regular feeding massively interferes with the mental state of the victim up to the point where their subconscious tries to fill in the blanks with stuff that makes more sense to a modern human than &amp;quot;I was attacked by a vampire&amp;quot;?<br /> And no, the blood bond makes no appearance here.<br /> <br /> The far greater problem is the age-old conspiracy with thousands of members anyway, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://phys.org/news/2016-01-equation-large-scale-conspiracies-quickly-reveal.html&amp;quot;]when</a> smaller modern conspiracies have unraveled after a few decades at most[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Kiss don't erase memory, dude. Stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T13:27:47-08:00","id":1286523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286432#post1286432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah that is why Blush of life solves it</div> </div> </div> </div>But that totally removes the point of the blurring as a benefit. It just means you have to spend buckets of blood every time you leave the haven, which means you're far more likely to get caught having to feed maybe three or four times as much as before, and you won't have the blur effect to protect you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T20:55:49-08:00","id":1286607,"title":"","content":"There are a number of reasons that the Masquerade IS sustainable:<br /> None of them are Mechanical to the system as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24037_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24037\" data-vbnamecard=\"24037\">Leandro16</a> suggests putting in or <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13136\" data-vbnamecard=\"13136\">Legendre</a> implemented in the Mush.<br /> <br /> The two Biggest ones <br /> <br /> <b>Firstly</b>, Vampires are Apex Predators, they are selfish first and foremost. While they can produce competitors in nearly an instant, and have desires to to for company or as allies, they are still producing Competitors for resources. &quot;Dumb animals&quot; won't do that, the beast won't do it and people would have to be pretty stupid to do it, even if they can.<br /> Even the Sabbat doesn't do it... where they live, just in other people's territory to fuck up that territory.<br /> <br /> There's nothing inherent stopping wolves from overpopulating, except supply of food and competition with other Predators, it doesn't take too long to have the populations find a homeostasis of sustainable predator levels without needing guidance from &quot;Intelligent&quot; creatures<br /> <br /> <b>Secondly,</b> The Hierarchy, especially Camarilla<br /> There is a phrase in management; &quot;Shit rolls downhill.&quot; and the kind of vampires that might, possibly think of this are at the bottom of the hill if not a valley even lower.<br /> If a large embrace hotspot exists that isn't dealt with, then the Justicar of a region will be drilled by the Inner Council*, the Prince gets drilled, Sherriff or Scourge is in deep, then the neonate and possibly their sire (depending if they are released or not) They should be watched to prevent this kind of thing before being released and should only be released if not stupid enough to do this kind of thing. It'll also possibly get the Primogen dirty depending on the city.<br /> Now, depending on how bad it is, anyone up to the Justicar could lose their role or even be executed for it, so all of them have the pressure from above to prevent it, and they will push that pressure to those below (Shit Rolling down Hill) to both prevent, and if needed, cover it up.<br /> <br /> So basically every position holder in the Camarilla that is upstream of the problem has a vested interest in preventing it, and the power to prevent it, or punish it if not prevented<br /> <br /> *The inner council almost certainly reports to others above the chain as well.<br /> <br /> <b>2b </b>The independants<br /> - They usually run a pretty tight ship, Giovanni, Assamite, Setite, their heirachy is so closely knit it won't be an issue.<br /> Ironically the Ravnos were probably more likely to be free with embracing, but that's not a problem any more is it? <br /> <br /> <b>2c</b> - The Sabbat<br /> Pragmatically, if embracing a lot becomes an issue (Outside of a Crusade) then they done fucked up, and someone will directly punish (Kill) them for making life hard for the elder. If it's not an issue; it's not an issue. Being more hands on, different cities will be different in their treatment, but that's a general rule for it. If a ranking member thinks there's too many in a city and feeding or hiding is getting hard, you purge the city in one way or another - False Sabbat rarely last long enough to become True Sabbat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T21:09:49-08:00","id":1286609,"title":"","content":"Also, What I consider to be a minor addendum compared to the rest - Even the Technocracy is constantly helping cover the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T21:31:11-08:00","id":1286612,"title":"","content":"Population control that\u2019s already in place:<br /> <br /> The book already says embraces don\u2019t always work. No need to add a homebrew mechanic unless you desire to. There isn\u2019t a listed reason but the first time it fails you can expect others to be careful (losing someone you care about from a botched embrace is emotionally devastating). <br /> <br /> Hunters and other supernaturals hunt kindred on the regular. No one is safe. <br /> <br /> Forced infighting by Camarilla and Sabbat keep younger populations down. (Plot potential)<br /> <br /> Hatfield and Clyde drama between clans keeps populations down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:32:15-08:00","id":1286722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286511#post1286511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiss don't erase memory, dude. Stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>This line of argument needs to end. No, it doesn't <i>erase</i> memory in and of itself, all it does and all it needs to do is <i>interfere</i> with the snack's memory.<br /> <br /> The Kiss forces a state of altered consciousness likened to orgasmic bliss or the euphoric haze of a good buzz or drug trip. This is RAW, as already described. This state of altered consciousness interferes with the mortal's memory, and this is also RAW as already described. Meanwhile...<br /> <br /> 1. Humans have a remarkable ability for rationalization and distorting their own memories, both in the long term and short term. If you've ever been drunk -- not even blackout drunk, just something more than a good buzz -- you should know exactly what I mean, especially if you've talked to those around you about what happened especially if they were <i>also</i> drunk. And, this is <i>not</i> a case of memory distortion and problematic recall in the case of altered consciousness; it happens <i>when completely sober</i>. If a mortal is fed from under careful circumstances, as RAW states and already discussed they're more likely than not to rationalize it in a way that makes sense to them and fits the social context of when they were fed from.<br /> <br /> RAW is and should be all you need, here. It's all in the manual. But, to put a finer point on it considering this won't die...<br /> <br /> 2. Vampires tend to feed when and where they can control the circumstances and cover their asses. That means Racks. Racks trend overwhelmingly towards being places where psychoactives, even those simple and ubiquitous as alcohol, flow freely in a socially-chaotic atmosphere. That means they attract mortals, lower their inhibitions and make them more pliant, which means feeding is overall easier and harder for third parties to track. It doesn't matter if the Rack in question is a skid row or a trendy night club, the circumstances tend to stay the same. The important part to all this being, mortals in Racks <i>tend to already have altered states of mind, divided attention, and possibly mild sensory overload, <b>before</b> the Kiss is applied which amplifies its effects while also providing a social context for the mortal to rationalize what happened to them after the fact</i>.<br /> <br /> And, lastly...<br /> <br /> 3. For reasons that should be obvious, being fed from causes, bare minimum, mild (acute) anemia. Most official sources I've read liken a single-BP feeding to a blood donation, but even that's enough to trigger (non-threatening) disorientation, lightheadedness, and nausea. Now, for that, see above; the symptoms of a feeding mimic hangover and/or mild withdrawal, and if the mortal had been at a Rack it's <i>more likely</i> for them to rationalize it as a wild night out than &quot;vampires did it&quot;. More than that...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Humans can lose approximately 15-20% of blood volume before suffering hypovolemic shock. Blood donation generally takes 8-10% of blood volume. This compares almost perfectly to that, by RAW, humans have 10 BP and can have 2 points taken before requiring emergency care.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ...and we are <i>definitely</i> talking more prominent and serious symptoms of anemia. Symptoms of anemia include <i>confusion</i>, <i>shortened attention span</i>, disorientation, light headedness, and depending upon type and severity, <i>memory disruption and loss</i>. Which makes absolute sense, because we're talking about a medical condition whereby the flow of oxygen to the brain is compromised.<br /> <br /> So, just to wrap this up...<br /> <br /> Most feedings occur in Racks or other places where mortals are likely to <i>already</i> be in altered states of mind, which interfere with memory. The Kiss alters consciousness in and of itself, which interferes with memory. And, the very act of feeding induces a medical condition which alters consciousness and perception, which can depending on severity interfere with memory. And still, <i>even after all that</i>, mortals' recollection of the event is going to change to recontextualize and rationalize it. It's going to take an <i>astoundingly</i> strong-willed mortal (WP 4+, easy) to overcome all that and remember enough to think <i>something</i> might have been weird about it.<br /> <br /> And <i>everything</i> I just mentioned hinges <i>entirely</i> on the notion the vampire did <i>no</i><i>thing</i> to the mortal other than give them the Kiss. No discipline use, no additional &quot;party favors&quot; or whatnot, no kinky shit, not even booping the mortal with a one-point blood bond. Although personally, I always house rule licking the wound from a Kiss induces the blood bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 02-11-2019, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:36:10-08:00","id":1286725,"title":"","content":"Kindred are incredibly violent and territorial to one another.<br /> <br /> That's their population control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T11:28:26-08:00","id":1286795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable#post1286419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanicaly the masquerade is unsustainable in all editions becuase of Two Factors<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>The Overpopulation of vampires </b>(Seriusly they are almost in every city , some of them has to fuck up)</li> <li><b>The vampires have no realiable way of camuflating feeding from his victims</b> (Orgasmic Bite is great to portray the sensuality of the vampire and stop the victim resisting but doesnt erase the memories of the moment).</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Um, unless something has changed in V5 that I missed, the vampiric population is under 50,000 world wide, and that is including all the vampires that are in torpor. Your average city won't have any vampires and in the cases where the mortal population is big enough, like say San Francisco, then you would have like 5 vampires total in the city. Overpopulation only occurs if the ST has decided to artificially inflate population numbers.<br /> <br /> As for feeding, last I checked you can lick a wound to auto heal the feeding punctures. All you have to do is pick victims that won't remember much, such as college kids at a party. After a few drinks they think they just got lucky and ended up with a hicky.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue for the Masquerade isn't undead population or feeding, it is technology. Things like facial recognition databases and city wide camera networks will eventually force any vampire over the age of say 20 years undead to either become a complete recluse or move to a third world country that lacks that sort of infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T14:08:34-08:00","id":1286836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286795#post1286795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, unless something has changed in V5 that I missed, the vampiric population is under 50,000 world wide, and that is including all the vampires that are in torpor. Your average city won't have any vampires and in the cases where the mortal population is big enough, like say San Francisco, then you would have like 5 vampires total in the city. Overpopulation only occurs if the ST has decided to artificially inflate population numbers.<br /> <br /> As for feeding, last I checked you can lick a wound to auto heal the feeding punctures. All you have to do is pick victims that won't remember much, such as college kids at a party. After a few drinks they think they just got lucky and ended up with a hicky.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue for the Masquerade isn't undead population or feeding, it is technology. Things like facial recognition databases and city wide camera networks will eventually force any vampire over the age of say 20 years undead to either become a complete recluse or move to a third world country that lacks that sort of infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact there are more vampires than 1 per 50.000 humans that is as I said best case scenerario , sabbat shovelhead survivors , caitiff popping out of nowhere just look chicago suddenly there are a group of 20 caitiff that no one semeed to know about.(Heck V5 even said that some places have a 1/3000 vampire ratio)<br /> <br /> When you have so many vampires needing to feed is just a matter of time until they fuck things up and are the victim puts 2 and 2 together , are caught by hunter or as you said technogy ,hence the need of a natural population control and sobrenatural adaptations to remain hidden like memory eraser kiss or some kind of distortion to hide from cameras becuase you still need certain population levels if you want to talk about courts and factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T14:12:55-08:00","id":1286839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286523#post1286523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that totally removes the point of the blurring as a benefit. It just means you have to spend buckets of blood every time you leave the haven, which means you're far more likely to get caught having to feed maybe three or four times as much as before, and you won't have the blur effect to protect you.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad , I forgot to mention that I would make the blush of life last a number of hours equal to humanity or extend the duration to all night to improve the hability to camuflage in the herd of vampires but maybe separating the Distortion Mechanic from the blush of life is a better idea.Thanks for the feedback","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T14:39:51-08:00","id":1286848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286795#post1286795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, unless something has changed in V5 that I missed, the vampiric population is under 50,000 world wide, and that is including all the vampires that are in torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about right. People love to extrapolate based upon global population, without realizing not everyone lives in cities (as of 2018 it's only 55%), but the commonly-cited canonical 100,000:1 ratio is for <i>cities</i>. Realistically, that assumes all cities are created equal (they're not) and have identical social, economic, and political benefits and challenges (they don't), while discounting the confounding effect urban sprawl, commuting and tourism, state and private surveillance, and security will have. Case in point, let's compare two cities on extreme ends of the spectrum: Rio de Janeiro and London.<br /> <br /> Rio is a huge fucking city with an estimated population 1.5 times that of London, with a massive tourism industry, unspeakable socioeconomic divides, globally-infamous corrupt police force, a crime rate so high the Brazilian government literally declared martial law last year, and only since then is any form of electronic surveillance being implemented. You could probably go down to 20,000:1 on the human-to-vampire ratio in some place like Rio.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the UK's a fucking police state and London is its crown jewel. What happened to London's vampire population in V5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T15:09:33-08:00","id":1286859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286848#post1286848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the UK's a fucking police state and London is its crown jewel. What happened to London's vampire population in V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't think i've ever heard the UK described as a police state before, generally everyone in the UK complains that there are far too few police. London may have been the world capital of CCTV cameras, but that's precisely because there are nowhere near enough police to cover it. That's real world, WoD London would be much worse","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T17:45:56-08:00","id":1286917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286859#post1286859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...London may have been the world capital of CCTV cameras, but that's precisely because there are nowhere near enough police to cover it...</div> </div> </div> </div>If it were merely a matter of CCTV cameras and physical law enforcement presence it would be an entirely different matter, but times have changed. Now it's about bulk data collection, automated aggregation, mandatory backdoor decryption for wireless devices, D-notice abuse and surveillance of journalists and politicians alike, voting register manipulation, and more recently surveillance and restriction of internet access and social media activity. It's to the point last year the ECHR declared the United Kingdom in violation of human rights on the back of the 2014 DRIPA and 2016 IPA, and the DRAR doesn't provide nearly enough oversight or transparency to act as an effective regulator on state surveillance power.<br /> <br /> Bare minimum, the Cameron government's attempt to kill the Snowden story in its crib by issuance of D-notices, and eventually raiding <i>The Guardian</i>'s office to oversee physical destruction of the outlet's storage devices, damn well should have been the shot heard round the world with regards to how seriously the contemporary UK government regards freedom of expression and the press. The Cameron government's reaction to it was nothing short of emetic and wholly inexcusable.<br /> <br /> But, I digress. The point being, the higher the level of surveillance and security, the higher that ratio should be for obvious reasons. That pans out in V5, and it well should be a consideration on the mind of any ST looking to run a VtM chronicle set in the 21st Century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T04:32:34-08:00","id":1287018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286722#post1286722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This line of argument needs to end. No, it doesn't <i>erase</i> memory in and of itself, all it does and all it needs to do is <i>interfere</i> with the snack's memory.<br /> <br /> The Kiss forces a state of altered consciousness likened to orgasmic bliss or the euphoric haze of a good buzz or drug trip. This is RAW, as already described. This state of altered consciousness interferes with the mortal's memory, and this is also RAW as already described. Meanwhile...<br /> <br /> 1. Humans have a remarkable ability for rationalization and distorting their own memories, both in the long term and short term. If you've ever been drunk -- not even blackout drunk, just something more than a good buzz -- you should know exactly what I mean, especially if you've talked to those around you about what happened especially if they were <i>also</i> drunk. And, this is <i>not</i> a case of memory distortion and problematic recall in the case of altered consciousness; it happens <i>when completely sober</i>. If a mortal is fed from under careful circumstances, as RAW states and already discussed they're more likely than not to rationalize it in a way that makes sense to them and fits the social context of when they were fed from.<br /> <br /> RAW is and should be all you need, here. It's all in the manual. But, to put a finer point on it considering this won't die...<br /> <br /> 2. Vampires tend to feed when and where they can control the circumstances and cover their asses. That means Racks. Racks trend overwhelmingly towards being places where psychoactives, even those simple and ubiquitous as alcohol, flow freely in a socially-chaotic atmosphere. That means they attract mortals, lower their inhibitions and make them more pliant, which means feeding is overall easier and harder for third parties to track. It doesn't matter if the Rack in question is a skid row or a trendy night club, the circumstances tend to stay the same. The important part to all this being, mortals in Racks <i>tend to already have altered states of mind, divided attention, and possibly mild sensory overload, <b>before</b> the Kiss is applied which amplifies its effects while also providing a social context for the mortal to rationalize what happened to them after the fact</i>.<br /> <br /> And, lastly...<br /> <br /> 3. For reasons that should be obvious, being fed from causes, bare minimum, mild (acute) anemia. Most official sources I've read liken a single-BP feeding to a blood donation, but even that's enough to trigger (non-threatening) disorientation, lightheadedness, and nausea. Now, for that, see above; the symptoms of a feeding mimic hangover and/or mild withdrawal, and if the mortal had been at a Rack it's <i>more likely</i> for them to rationalize it as a wild night out than &quot;vampires did it&quot;. More than that...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Humans can lose approximately 15-20% of blood volume before suffering hypovolemic shock. Blood donation generally takes 8-10% of blood volume. This compares almost perfectly to that, by RAW, humans have 10 BP and can have 2 points taken before requiring emergency care.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ...and we are <i>definitely</i> talking more prominent and serious symptoms of anemia. Symptoms of anemia include <i>confusion</i>, <i>shortened attention span</i>, disorientation, light headedness, and depending upon type and severity, <i>memory disruption and loss</i>. Which makes absolute sense, because we're talking about a medical condition whereby the flow of oxygen to the brain is compromised.<br /> <br /> So, just to wrap this up...<br /> <br /> Most feedings occur in Racks or other places where mortals are likely to <i>already</i> be in altered states of mind, which interfere with memory. The Kiss alters consciousness in and of itself, which interferes with memory. And, the very act of feeding induces a medical condition which alters consciousness and perception, which can depending on severity interfere with memory. And still, <i>even after all that</i>, mortals' recollection of the event is going to change to recontextualize and rationalize it. It's going to take an <i>astoundingly</i> strong-willed mortal (WP 4+, easy) to overcome all that and remember enough to think <i>something</i> might have been weird about it.<br /> <br /> And <i>everything</i> I just mentioned hinges <i>entirely</i> on the notion the vampire did <i>no</i><i>thing</i> to the mortal other than give them the Kiss. No discipline use, no additional &quot;party favors&quot; or whatnot, no kinky shit, not even booping the mortal with a one-point blood bond. Although personally, I always house rule licking the wound from a Kiss induces the blood bond.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I absolutely, 100% agree with this post and will shamelessly quote myself from an earlier discussion on the topic:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eddie Fiori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1174479-how-do-feeding-without-getting-caught?p=1174612#post1174612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always house ruled that the Kiss produces a low level type of amnesia.<br /> <br /> 1. It's the only way I can even remotely begin to justify the continued existence of the Masquerade, and<br /> 2. Less time spent on stocking up on chloroform, breaking into butcher shops/blood banks, or getting rid of bodies leaves us with more time for role playing the encounter itself. I want feeding to be about role play, not jumping through elaborate hoops.<br /> <br /> The way we play, the Kiss clouds the victim's memories in a rough period of three to five minutes before and after the Kiss itself. The victim will then usually rationalize what happened based on the setting (except, of course, for when full or partial recollection would be dramatically correct).<br /> <br /> A sensual Kiss in a club, late at night? &quot;Damn, where did the cute guy go?, Shit, my head is spinning, I've must have had too much to drink. Did someone spike my drink?&quot;<br /> An unexpected and sudden Kiss in a dirty alley? &quot;Uuuh, what happened? Was I mugged?&quot;<br /> <br /> Et cetera.<br /> <br /> Of course, no Kiss will save a Kindred who blatantly reveals his true nature before the act or otherwise neglects basic tradecraft. Such an act is bound to be remembered.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:31:10-08:00","id":1287375,"title":"","content":"Overpopulation has stated to be an issue for vampires since the beginning of the franchise with 100 vampires in Chicago being considerable unstainable.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I ruled that there were 150,000 vampires in 2018.<br /> <br /> Except the Second Inquisition, Gehenna Crusade, Beckoning, and MYSTERIOUS CIRCUMSTANCES has wiped out 75K globally so its now back to &quot;manageable&quot; levels with some vampires believing its the end.<br /> <br /> The answer to the question, &quot;How did the Masquerade survive?&quot;<br /> <br /> The answer being, &quot;Not well.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T11:48:34-08:00","id":1288963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286511#post1286511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiss don't erase memory, dude. Stop.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;only <b>remember</b> the encounter as a <b>drug trip</b>, [...]<b> interlude of weird rough sex</b>, [...] <b>delirious fog</b> </i><i><b>happy hallucination</b> [...] </i><i><b>blissed-out screen memory</b></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> No one is saying that the Kiss erases all memory of the encounter. It is the explicit text of VtM, however, that the Kiss &quot;blurs&quot; and confuses memories, and that people fill in the gaps with something more believable. This is why blood dolls and frequent victims aren't a huge Masquerade breach.<br /> <br /> You can say that that text is dumb or poorly written or that the books don't bring enough attention to it, but it's definitely there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T14:36:47-08:00","id":1289313,"title":"","content":"What I dont like is that I apparently came to the table at a time when Vampire is, seemingly ending, being hunted on all sides by all supernaturals is not as fun as the old game sounded to me...<br /> <br /> Looks like the future is Werewolf... sadly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T19:26:51-08:00","id":1289382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talvas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1289313#post1289313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I dont like is that I apparently came to the table at a time when Vampire is, seemingly ending, being hunted on all sides by all supernaturals is not as fun as the old game sounded to me...<br /> <br /> Looks like the future is Werewolf... sadly...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's where it always has been. It was like that in 1991 and if you look at the DA line it was like that in the 1200s... and yet there are still kindred. People want monsters to rule the world.. because deep down they need to believe that something is responsible for all the bad things that happen to them. That is why the Masquerade will never &quot;Fall&quot; its why the solution to the SI is the same as the first Inquisition. Let them kill a bunch of kindred reposition society use it as an excuse for why things are the way they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T21:13:28-08:00","id":1289408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable#post1286419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanicaly the masquerade is unsustainable in all editions becuase of Two Factors<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>The Overpopulation of vampires </b>(Seriusly they are almost in every city , some of them has to fuck up)</li> <li><b>The vampires have no realiable way of camuflating feeding from his victims</b> (Orgasmic Bite is great to portray the sensuality of the vampire and stop the victim resisting but doesnt erase the memories of the moment).</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>The Masquerade was never sustainable. <br /> <br /> Let's assume that every vampire ever practices all of the caution and secrecy of a master spy in their nightly unlives and that shovelheads and abandoned fledglings aren't a thing. There have been <a href=\"https://motherboard.vice.com/en_us/article/aekwjb/this-math-shows-how-long-itd-take-vampires-to-run-out-of-human-blood-to-drink\" target=\"_blank\">academic studies</a> into whether the earth's human population could feasibly sustain a coexisting population of vampires. Most of these studies assume that vampires are butchers on the scale of Salem's Lot or John Carpenter's Vampires and would drive humanity extinct within a relatively short time frame.<br /> <br /> There was <a href=\"http://www.m-hikari.com/ams/ams-2013/ams-9-12-2013/strielkowskiAMS9-12-2013.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">one particular study</a>, though, which examined three separate models of vampiric predation upon humankind: Salem's Lot-level butchery, Anne Rice-level restraint (where vampires don't have to kill when they feed, but sometimes do), and True Blood-level restraint (where vampires have a viable alternative to human blood, but sometimes Embrace humans). The conclusion was that Anne Rice's vampires would still depopulate the planet within 60 or so years, unless the population of vampires remained inordinately small. <br /> <br /> The (literal) statistical variables in the World of Darkness are considerably different than in Anne Rice's world. But I feel safe in saying the WoD is an even less sustainable environment for humans and vampires to coexist in than Anne Rice's setting is. <br /> <br /> Vampires' nightly blood demands are essentially the WoD's faster than light space travel. This is just one area of the setting where we have to suspend our disbelief.<br /> <br /> Whether the setting would <i>feel</i> more believable with fewer vampires and better built-in camouflage methods is a separate matter, though. But given what the numbers bear out, this is just one area where we're still squinting our eyes and saying &quot;fooh-fooh&quot; to the science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T22:12:43-08:00","id":1289422,"title":"","content":"The Rice Model assumes a 10% of death per feeding, and 10% of deaths being embraced, but they can feed once a week.<br /> At the very worst Kindred in WoD are killing 10% of feeding. That's someone only draining a mortal when down 10 blood because they like to kill. And you probably won't have that psychopath embracing every 10th one as well. You only do anything like that in War.<br /> <br /> <b>Real world maths</b> -<br /> A blood donation (approx 1 bloodpoint) is recovered in full for blood volume in about 28 days. The red blood cells only mature after 3 months, which is why there's a delay on allowing you to donate blood more often.<br /> So a Vampire can exist on a herd of 28 vessels if all stay healthy.<br /> <br /> <b>In Game Maths/Mechanics</b><br /> The 1 level of damage dealt by draining a blood point is healed by (most) mortals after one day of rest.<br /> As such, if just feeding for daily waking, you can have a herd of 1 and survive while they stay healthy.<br /> (Look at the Impundulu Bloodline weakness, it relies on this mechanic)<br /> <br /> <br /> *Using a Study is only as good as the assumptions used to create the study","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T00:32:09-08:00","id":1289441,"title":"","content":"1. Does it need to be fixed? Some things are fine to be explained away in non-mechanical terms. <br /> 2. Reliably is hard to pin down. I mean, not only is there a kiss, Dominate, Presence, bribery, and killing exist. Plus people in the Camarilla whose job it is to ensure the Masquerade. Plus the generally worse/more corrupt nature of WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T03:18:55-08:00","id":1289455,"title":"","content":"V5 whole premise is that the Masquerade is shattered. The Inquisition does obfuscate the truth from the wider public for really inane reasons. (at least according to the Cam book) but the fact remain that people in power know of vampires.<br /> <br /> And if they don't that simply mean someone else is withholding intell for see above reasons.<br /> <br /> Anyway the Masquerade being unsustainable is now WAD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:02:47-08:00","id":1289501,"title":"","content":"V5 isn't holding to the Masquerade being shattered. It is cracked, yes, but not completely gone. The SI doesn't know the identities of every vampire in existence, it gleaned the existence of the Tremere and Giovanni. The fact that the general public is still in the dark about the supernatural shows that the masquerade is still very much intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T12:47:38-08:00","id":1289614,"title":"","content":"Mortals knowing that vampires exist is what breaks the Masquerade not them knowing every vampire in existence. And considering that the Inquisition is supposed to have an absolute technological edge over the Camarilla (which is how they did stuff like cracking Shrecknet for exemple) they have more than enough proof to reveal the existence vampires to everyone else if (when?) they so desire.<br /> <br /> So yes the Masquerade is shattered because it is no longer in the hands of kindreds to sustain it. Any rogue agent of the Inquisition could reveal the existence of vampire.<br /> <br /> On the bright side however since its basically gone there is less risk in breaking the Masquerade nowadays. Since the main risk of revealing the existence of vampire already happened: the SI which will cover the breach for you before knocking on the door to erase you and everyone else in town.<br /> <br /> So yes in an ironic and kind of absurd way the Inquisition is the main enforcer of the Masquerade at least until they stop being stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 02-19-2019, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:03:58-08:00","id":1289648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286848#post1286848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile, the UK's a fucking police state and London is its crown jewel. What happened to London's vampire population in V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, London has serious issues with crime, even violent crime. Not on the 3rd world level, of course, but high in the developed world. People seriously overestimate those technologies, we're not already in that kind of sci-fi dystopia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:24:39-08:00","id":1289667,"title":"","content":"Mortals knew of vampires existing before the SI became a thing. Hunters are a prime example, not to mention ghouls and other mortal servants. Even with just those examples, which falls under your &quot;mortals knowing they exist means the masquerade is shattered&quot; the masquerade has been seen as intact. It's when the general populace knows they exist that the masquerade becomes broken.<br /> <br /> The camarilla still has a hold on the masquerade, which is why it still exists. They may have thrown the tremere under the bus, but they still maintain control as feeding misinformation to the SI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:33:47-08:00","id":1289673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1289614#post1289614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals knowing that vampires exist is what breaks the Masquerade not them knowing every vampire in existence. And considering that the Inquisition is supposed to have an absolute technological edge over the Camarilla (which is how they did stuff like cracking Shrecknet for exemple) they have more than enough proof to reveal the existence vampires to everyone else if (when?) they so desire.<br /> <br /> So yes the Masquerade is shattered because it is no longer in the hands of kindreds to sustain it. Any rogue agent of the Inquisition could reveal the existence of vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>So where is the difference to before? The Society of Leopold was part of VtM since first edition and the whole &quot;blankbody&quot; stuff arose from intelligence agency plot seeds that were there at least from Revised, if not earlier. The only thing that's changed is that the setting has moved forward from &quot;we'd be fucked if they managed to convince anyone actually powerful and completely fucked if they convinced humanity&quot; to &quot;we <i>are </i>fucked, but not completely fucked&quot;. Considering that the Society of Leopold had captive vampires since at least Revised that they could theoretically have presented to anyone who bothered with them, your complaints are about 20 years too late.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1289614#post1289614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yes in an ironic and kind of absurd way the Inquisition is the main enforcer of the Masquerade at least until they stop being stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>While revealing the vampires would make sense, not revealing them IMO is not so non-sensical that that it would stretch my suspension of disbelief. In the end, we are talking about spooks here. People who tend to be conservative, preferring the known terror over the terror of the unknown. Revealing the existence of vampires to the world would be absolute chaos. Noone knows what would happen - would it be a quiet cleanup? Would there be rioting in the streets? Lynch mobs staking their odd neighbours? Would some of the vampires actually manage to turn public opinion around and present themselves as misunderstood and persecuted?<br /> <br /> The way it currently is, though? London and Vienna have fallen, as have several Sabbat fortresses. The SI believes it is winning. Why rock the boat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:12:57-08:00","id":1289688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1289673#post1289673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So where is the difference to before? The Society of Leopold was part of VtM since first edition and the whole &quot;blankbody&quot; stuff arose from intelligence agency plot seeds that were there at least from Revised, if not earlier. The only thing that's changed is that the setting has moved forward from &quot;we'd be fucked if they managed to convince anyone actually powerful and completely fucked if they convinced humanity&quot; to &quot;we <i>are </i>fucked, but not completely fucked&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Masquerade does not hinder hunters like before that's the difference. Also vampires have completely lost control over the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering that the Society of Leopold had captive vampires since at least Revised that they could theoretically have presented to anyone who bothered with them, your complaints are about 20 years too late. </div> </div> </div>I am not denying that plot holes can not exist in previous editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While revealing the vampires would make sense, not revealing them IMO is not so non-sensical that that it would stretch my suspension of disbelief. In the end, we are talking about spooks here. People who tend to be conservative, preferring the known terror over the terror of the unknown. Revealing the existence of vampires to the world would be absolute chaos. Noone knows what would happen - would it be a quiet cleanup? Would there be rioting in the streets? Lynch mobs staking their odd neighbours? Would some of the vampires actually manage to turn public opinion around and present themselves as misunderstood and persecuted? </div> </div> </div>Maybe for you it works but not for me. When you are ready to kill/manipulate innocent to get to vampires the excuses not to reveal as you mention fall flat. I mean the fear of chaos really ? Nah I don't buy it a single second.<br /> <br /> And the last one is just completely is just completely stupid in my pov.<br /> Remember how your country went to war (twice) 'cause a few lunatics blew some tower ? Now imagine what the revelation that eldritch monstruosities with the power to dominate mind and other spooky stuff would actually cause as a reaction. I am sure the let's give vampire rights movement would be the last threat to the vampiricides would have to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way it currently is, though? London and Vienna have fallen, as have several Sabbat fortresses. The SI believes it is winning. Why rock the boat? </div> </div> </div>Because we can win easier and faster ? And more importantly get rid of what hold the vampires have left in mortal institutions which is basically game over for the Camarilla ? Plus the fact that and the Society of Leopold should know that that if the secret is leak the licks can never recover as vampires would not be forgotten this time unlike in DA.<br /> <br /> Plus as far as I am concerned the Inquisition has nothing to lose here. And SO MUCH to gain. I mean just imagine if every cop, every soldier... NO every mortal on the planet was a potential vampire hunter. Oh yeah I know how to call this. Gehenna mortal style.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also the very fact that the Inquisiton actually maintain the Masquerade actually creates plot problems of its own. Like in books it says they cover their strikes by painting them to be terrorist attack... .<br /> <br /> Like really ? really ? Terrorist attacks ?<br /> <br /> Remember me what get a ton of media/agency/political attention when it happens in the west ? Yuuup terrorist attacks. It's honestly the worst excuse the devs could have imagined as a cover. Cause you can be sure that the Inquisition will get all non-informed agency on their ass as well as the political power of multiple countries that will do their best to hinder that &quot;terrorist organisation&quot;.<br /> <br /> Notwithstanding journalists that will investigate on their side to uncover what actually happened and try to link all those supposed terrorist attacks.<br /> That's a helluva of people to fool. And not necessarily the most gullible groups.<br /> <br /> And again any rogue hunter could destroy the Masquerade irreversibly. Anyone.<br /> <br /> I could go on and on, on this topic but yeah it doesn't work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 02-19-2019, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T17:10:08-08:00","id":1289706,"title":"","content":"I think that the two of you are more arguing on the definition of the Masquerade rather than what the situation is in present.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24936\" data-vbnamecard=\"24936\">Morbus</a> - The Argument that it's not &quot;Broken&quot; is that it's not public knowledge that Vampires exist, they're still working to cover up their activities from the general populace.<br /> Yes, this is the worst situation for vampires being hunted since the times of the Inquisition (When Vampires realized the need for Masquerade instead of Silence-of-the-blood) but in general if someone on the street says that they &quot;Saw a Vampire&quot; or their defense for killing someone was that &quot;they were a vampire&quot; then they're still treated as crazy, because the truth isn't in public awareness yet.<br /> <br /> If the Masquerade was &quot;Broken&quot; completely, then the protections that Vampires do wouldn't help hide them because the secret is out. Like the Sookie Stackhouse series of books and TV - Vampires are out of the coffin, if you say &quot;A Vampire kidnapped me&quot; the police investigate it instead of throwing you in an asylum.<br /> <br /> I think that the intent of the designers is to make everyone more aware that it's an issue and _close_ to breaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T17:15:16-08:00","id":1289710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talvas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1289313#post1289313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I dont like is that I apparently came to the table at a time when Vampire is, seemingly ending, being hunted on all sides by all supernaturals is not as fun as the old game sounded to me...<br /> <br /> Looks like the future is Werewolf... sadly...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes honestly I'm seeing a lot of random detritus getting in the way of the story. The classic comparison for me is how VtM: Bloodlines handles feeding compared with how V5 handles feeding. VtMB has a huge plot all about plaguebearers and how careless feeding spreads these diseases. Both the Anarchs and Tremere want you to look into it, and both reveal a lot about themselves and how they view the other when you engage with those offers. You learn a lot about the strengths and weaknesses of both groups from such a simple thing. We're seeing how feeding habits, hunting domain, and the &quot;ecology&quot; of Vampires mix together to give a story. The whole thing is about feeding, but in a very abstract sense.<br /> <br /> As you go through you discover more is afoot, and uncover a huge cult of world-ending vampiric typhoid maries.<br /> <br /> Compare with how V5 seemingly wants you to devote endless RP and rolls to... feeding on individual kine? In relatively normal situations? Oh boy, I do remember my favourite thing in VtMB, the bit where I ran into a nightclub to drink for a few seconds from a dancer and then leave again. What excitement. Such a bracing story.<br /> <br /> Same goes RE hunters. Wider narratives should trump a ubiquitous hunter menace.<br /> <br /> Think about it like a movie set on an island. Focus on the wider issue of reliably getting clean water, reliably getting fresh food, and figuring out how to defend yourselves. Don't focus on the minutia once a system is in place. So when a Vampire feeds it should be an issue of functionality. Conflicts over ACCESS to feeding, over the safety and reliability of feeding; those are real stories! &quot;You can't do that, it's so obvious. Hunters will find you.&quot; The drama that unfolds from finding a new niche when your old one isn't possible, and having to learn new skills. V5 seems to have lost sight of that. And it applies to everything else too, sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T17:55:09-08:00","id":1289722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1289710#post1289710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think about it like a movie set on an island. Focus on the wider issue of reliably getting clean water, reliably getting fresh food, and figuring out how to defend yourselves. Don't focus on the minutia once a system is in place. So when a Vampire feeds it should be an issue of functionality. Conflicts over ACCESS to feeding, over the safety and reliability of feeding; those are real stories! &quot;You can't do that, it's so obvious. Hunters will find you.&quot; The drama that unfolds from finding a new niche when your old one isn't possible, and having to learn new skills. V5 seems to have lost sight of that. And it applies to everything else too, sadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great comparison.<br /> <br /> I want to know how someone built the well/ sourced a clean spring, not every time they go to grab a drink from that well.<br /> <br /> Even the stories of extreme survival - Drinking Turtle blood (<a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2014/01/mans-16-month-survival-sea/357607/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theatlantic.com/internat...al-sea/357607/</a> ) it may be stressful on a day to day basis, but once you have something that works, focusing on it as a daily struggle isn't interesting to play through.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:38:43-08:00","id":1289737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1289722#post1289722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a great comparison.<br /> <br /> I want to know how someone built the well/ sourced a clean spring, not every time they go to grab a drink from that well.<br /> <br /> Even the stories of extreme survival - Drinking Turtle blood (<a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2014/01/mans-16-month-survival-sea/357607/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theatlantic.com/internat...al-sea/357607/</a> ) it may be stressful on a day to day basis, but once you have something that works, focusing on it as a daily struggle isn't interesting to play through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Drama unfolds when some Sabbat thugs think they can feed in your bar. Your patrons are possibly like your cattle or your family. Maybe a mixture. How do you handle this? How do you handle the hunters they attract if you're too meek to confront them? How do you handle the Sabbat retaliating if you tell them to beat it? And once you've sorted this issue, it's better for the story if it stays sorted... unless some clever complication unsorts it, and that's new drama. A clever Grimaldi pencil-pusher notices that you're not completely up to date on your taxes, and manages to go over the head of anyone you've manipulated with the blood bond or presence. Now there's a warrant out for your arrest and your bar is shut down as part of the investigation. All because some ghoul wants to make a splash and impress a pack you pissed off, and you will probably never even find out who they are... unless you're clever and resourceful, or ready to beat a lot of answers out of people.<br /> <br /> THOSE are all really natural organic stories about these &quot;urban predators&quot;. I don't care for bean-counting when it comes to special kinds of blood from different sorts of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:43:16-08:00","id":1290036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1289710#post1289710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes honestly I'm seeing a lot of random detritus getting in the way of the story. The classic comparison for me is how VtM: Bloodlines handles feeding compared with how V5 handles feeding. VtMB has a huge plot all about plaguebearers and how careless feeding spreads these diseases. Both the Anarchs and Tremere want you to look into it, and both reveal a lot about themselves and how they view the other when you engage with those offers. You learn a lot about the strengths and weaknesses of both groups from such a simple thing. We're seeing how feeding habits, hunting domain, and the &quot;ecology&quot; of Vampires mix together to give a story. The whole thing is about feeding, but in a very abstract sense.<br /> <br /> As you go through you discover more is afoot, and uncover a huge cult of world-ending vampiric typhoid maries.<br /> <br /> Compare with how V5 seemingly wants you to devote endless RP and rolls to... feeding on individual kine? In relatively normal situations? Oh boy, I do remember my favourite thing in VtMB, the bit where I ran into a nightclub to drink for a few seconds from a dancer and then leave again. What excitement. Such a bracing story.<br /> <br /> Same goes RE hunters. Wider narratives should trump a ubiquitous hunter menace.<br /> <br /> Think about it like a movie set on an island. Focus on the wider issue of reliably getting clean water, reliably getting fresh food, and figuring out how to defend yourselves. Don't focus on the minutia once a system is in place. So when a Vampire feeds it should be an issue of functionality. Conflicts over ACCESS to feeding, over the safety and reliability of feeding; those are real stories! &quot;You can't do that, it's so obvious. Hunters will find you.&quot; The drama that unfolds from finding a new niche when your old one isn't possible, and having to learn new skills. V5 seems to have lost sight of that. And it applies to everything else too, sadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. I'm saying since the development, practically, that this whole focusing on blood and feeding is misleading. It sounds convincing that &quot;this is the core of the vampiric experience&quot; and stuff like that. It's great when a movie focuses on it in a good way (like Only Lovers Left Alive showed the rush caused by drinking the blood), or when you're playing a one-shot LARP, focusing on it, or a suchlike tabletop game, or the first few sessions as a new vampire player. It's also always a good thing to write fluff about, to establish the mood.<br /> <br /> But if it was a tv series about vampires, would you like to see that much focus on simple feeding <i>in every episode</i>? Seriously, people would already groan seeing it the fifth time.<br /> <br /> The reality is: things like that are boring as hell, on the long run, as a central game element, no matter the system behind it. Why? Because it's basic sustenance, you're doing all-the-fucking-time. That's why. It's a thing you do to be able to do the more interesting stuff. Yes, it's fun to do a detailed feeding scene, with all the hunting and/or seduction once in a while, but when you're forced, or expected to do them all the time, it starts losing its sheen pretty fast and let's face it, most groups will just handwave it away.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T16:07:06-08:00","id":1290129,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty easy to turn those feeding scenes into rolls at any point. I think there are even example rolls in the book? There certainly are on my Mr Gone Character Sheet\u2122 &quot;)<br /> <br /> An Alleycat player can just go &quot;I find a victim&quot; &quot;ok roll wits + streetwise and then strength + brawl to bash them on the head&quot;. It can be as in depth or brisk as you like, to the point of &quot;ok, before meeting up at the haven you all go and hunt, reduce your hunger to 1&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25038-tubect","name":"Tubect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:21:04-07:00","id":1299963,"title":"","content":"Most vampires embraced have a sire. That sire teaches them how to feed discreetly. Usually takes YEARS under their tutelage before you are released as a neonate, sometimes DECADES. Then, there is the masquerade.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade involves elders if great power LITERALLY KILLING vampires who don't know how to feed properly and break the masquerade. So the loose ones that fall through the cracks, the ones without proper training are routinely KILLED or taken in by a mentor. Ever hear of a Sheriff? That's his job. Clean up the mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:24:51-07:00","id":1300589,"title":"","content":"1. to me sustainability isn't the goal, outliving the other kindred who can't keep their nose clean is.<br /> <br /> 2. This is why you hunt smarter, which v5 emphasizes that need to, which ties into #1.<br /> <br /> - Generations shouldn't be removed, at most deemphasized, generation is still dictating of some elements of V5/Vampires such as siring and also how high some powers can go. Also I believe it should take some emphasis in the organized clans &amp; sects where generation has always mattered.<br /> <br /> - I'm of the belief that embracing should come at a cost, namely it should kick start your hunger (like automatically getting hunger points) or more extreme, should cost you experience. in the former it stops people from being able to do it willy nilly out of nowhere, in the latter it does that AND it has you as player/character investing into this new kindred with something you can't get back without it being as extreme as humanity or willpower. I say extreme as if you're trying to save someone who's otherwise dying or willingly wishes to be embraced, giving/losing humanity feels a bit high of a cost for saving someone's life/doing what they requested. In the case of willpower that's also potentially a high cost as well and it's effecting your character's ability to function as they were before the embrace.<br /> <br /> - Kiss should remain the same, at most alter it slighly due to the nature and intimacy of the act, if it comes as the result of violence I think it should be a traumatic moment for most, similar to an assault of any kind even if they're vague on the details. If it comes as the result of a night out hook up deal, then it should feel kind of just bleh/mixed on it. and of course in the POV of a blood doll, it should be kind of the rush. <br /> <br /> - Distortion and everything should be rather per clan basis, some should rather be self reliant on their own abilities (like gangrel's natural physical speed and agility or Nos' stealth focus and technology centric identity) while some can use tech or make up techniques to hide in plain sight and others should have natural repellant to it due to disciplines/clan advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13247-incognito","name":"InCogNito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T08:10:53-07:00","id":1302828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InCogNito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1300589#post1300589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- I'm of the belief that embracing should come at a cost, namely it should kick start your hunger (like automatically getting hunger points) or more extreme, should cost you experience. in the former it stops people from being able to do it willy nilly out of nowhere, in the latter it does that AND it has you as player/character investing into this new kindred with something you can't get back without it being as extreme as humanity or willpower. I say extreme as if you're trying to save someone who's otherwise dying or willingly wishes to be embraced, giving/losing humanity feels a bit high of a cost for saving someone's life/doing what they requested. In the case of willpower that's also potentially a high cost as well and it's effecting your character's ability to function as they were before the embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Embracing already comes at a cost. Congratulations. Now you have a kid. Saddled with a child, how is that not a cost or a burden?<br /> <br /> Chances are, that baby will die before it is an adult anyway. Vampires love to meet the sun when they're young. Many vampires don't survive to adulthood (Neonate status) because they kill themselves or they prove to not be good enough. When you embrace, you need to remember that one day you might have to <i>Reclaim The Blood</i>. Also... I thought there were many cities where you have to ask the eldest (or the Prince) if you can Embrace someone.<br /> <br /> I think Embracing is a non-issue. Doesn't need to come at a cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. If a Vampire embraces willy-nilly, he deserves to get whacked. And so does his progeny. And in any good city, that is a sure thing. Again, a non-issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T20:27:30-07:00","id":1302992,"title":"","content":"One of the things to remember is most vampires don't WANT to make multiple vampires because--really, what is the benefit unless you plan to send a bunch as enslaved cannon fodder to bum rush a stronger vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T11:18:59-07:00","id":1303134,"title":"","content":"I think the Masquerade is unsustainable for the same reason Batman defies logic and reason for being a viable concept. When I was a kid most people got the news/information from the broadcast networks, and newspapers. These were very controllable institutions.<br /> <br /> Technology has changed the way we gather and distribute information and things like the masquerade don't really seem possible. As someone else put it sometimes you just need to play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T14:15:47-07:00","id":1303180,"title":"","content":"The point is not that the Big Bad Vampire at command will rost your guts if you endanger the masquerade that\u00b4s just a patch (look at all those caitiff and fedding victims)<br /> <br /> The point is that when you have an population of at least 100.000 vampires who ocasionally flip the table and with more than the half of them without means of reliable fedding there is no way to explain why there is still masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T14:21:34-07:00","id":1303181,"title":"","content":"Heck from game design perspective you want vampires to have the ability to feed without leaving evidence unless there are witness aside of the victim or cameras<br /> <br /> Not having a mind wipe bite for low WP victims like the delirium should be a flaw not the norm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T15:59:17-07:00","id":1303207,"title":"","content":"V1 to V20 included no explicit feeding memory manipulation, though it sometimes implied one. V5 has one, as explicit as it gets.<br /> I can quote the passage a fourth time, but do I really have to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T16:24:51-07:00","id":1303214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1303207#post1303207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V1 to V20 included no explicit feeding memory manipulation, though it sometimes implied one. V5 has one, as explicit as it gets.<br /> I can quote the passage a fourth time, but do I really have to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vague Dark poetry isnt a mechanic and &quot;as far as I am concerned&quot; the mind erasing thing in V5 is a Dominate 1 thing a discipline that only 4 of 13 clans have","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 04-06-2019, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T01:45:08-07:00","id":1307715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1286422#post1286422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game you want already exist: VtR. Please let Requiem be Requiem, and Masquerade be Masquerade. I want Gen. I want Antes. I want Cain. I don't want deux ex machina amnesia bite neither deux ex machina glitch on cameras/mirror.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This, just this. It is as accurate as it gets.<br /> <br /> <br /> Masquerade has it faults, the whole Classic World of Darkness was not very well thought initially, but it is compelling, it got tons of lore, and a dedicated fan base.<br /> <br /> Do I like all the crossover lore inconsistencies? Do I like that is not really well designed for splat interaction? No and no, but again it is your game, each one was supposed to be played in isolation, no other splats stealing the spot light.<br /> <br /> If someone wants different mechanics, then please use Chronicles of Darkness, those are REALLY well thought, and use whatever background setting floats your boat (the <b>Translation Guide</b> is your best bet)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-26-2019, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T05:29:49-07:00","id":1307728,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that the feeding process was supposed to be even more euphoric than sex, and most mortals who casually experience it become dazed after the process. Having little to no memory of what the vampire actually did to them.<br /> <br /> And if we go by the population theory that there is 1 vampire for every 50k to 100k humans, and divide that up by the 7.5 billion humans currently estimated to be on earth right now, we only come away with a grand total of 75k to 150k vampires. That's enough to populate a large town, or a small city. Now that might sound like a lot at first, but you have to remember that this population is scattered all over the planet, as opposed to being clustered together in a single area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T12:20:42-07:00","id":1400157,"title":"","content":"Sorry life has been a while but I had to do a lot of things away from this fourm, so as suppper late reply<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1302828#post1302828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embracing already comes at a cost. Congratulations. Now you have a kid. Saddled with a child, how is that not a cost or a burden?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because not every Clan works by that logic. In fact my preferred clan, Gangrel, specifically says in lore:They choose to embrace sometimes ON THE SPOT just because they feel the person is strong enough, then they leave them for a year to fend for themselves, if they die they die. Does that sound like a cost? No, does that sound like a burden? Not personally.<br /> <br /> Neither is it in the case of embracing someone as a favor so they're not potentially a thinblood and let that person raise that new childe, similar to being a surrogate carrying a child to term for another person/family.<br /> <br /> I can think of several more ways that are not a &quot;you have a kid/person relies on you&quot;. <br /> <br /> I personally a fan of the more student teacher relationship for kindred, then the parent/child, especially for my clan of choice in that if the student wishes to drop out,go their own way or learn from another. I have nothing against your way though.<br /> <br /> As for your P.S. that's your sects thing, I'm much more classic Anarch and Sabbat leaning on embracing, it happens like an accidental pregnancy, sometimes and it's okay as long as someone else picks up the slack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13247-incognito","name":"InCogNito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T06:32:54-07:00","id":1400510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1302992#post1302992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things to remember is most vampires don't WANT to make multiple vampires because--really, what is the benefit unless you plan to send a bunch as enslaved cannon fodder to bum rush a stronger vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>This whas even said in a V20 sourcebook of how those rare non Giovanni Family embraces are happening.<br /> Well in one of my DA20 chronicles it has happened that an Autarkis Caitiff Elder did something to recover from his power loosing with the migration period because it whas from his perspective more important to save time and get stronger faster to be secured when some other cainite decide to just us him and his child as a stepladder to greater power. Well the plan worked and he secured a half dozen cainite knights to get an upstart power while later having ghouls as squires that get knighted with an embrace if one of the last knights where killed or they learned everything they could and so it would be a waste to not embrace such a talented person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T09:29:13-07:00","id":1400531,"title":"","content":"Came in to see a sequel to my own masquerade thread. Completely dissapointed.<br /> <br /> 1- Most drinks are done during a moment of passion or to someone unconscious. Person needs to be a victim during the few times this is not the case.<br /> 2- People have to rationalise an attack they were aware of as something of vampiric origin.<br /> 3- People have to conclude somehow that they have something to gain from spreading this story and nothing to lose.<br /> 4- Person needs evidence<br /> 5- person needs to give this story to a media outlet who's big enough to influence people but also which needs to go through it's own process of being taken seriously and not being squashed, which is a far more extensive process than 1-4.<br /> 6- News needs to be possitioned in a way that attracts attention and not put in a little box ten pages in.<br /> 7- readers have to take this media outlet seriously<br /> 8-At no point during this process a vampire steps in.<br /> <br /> <br /> So like, let's just imagine there's a very generous 1/8 chance that each step goes towards breaching the masquerade. All together that's a<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>.0000000596046448% </b>chance of a serious masquerade breach per feeding. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-02-2020, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T17:18:41-07:00","id":1400601,"title":"","content":"I have the feeling that i spoke the truth that everyone knew but also refused to acknowledge with this post and now some people are in negation phase<br /> <br /> The masquerade never was sustainable we just handwaved how things worked becuase we just wanted to tell an story , a lot of us assumed or better said houseruled that the kiss erases the memory something that is explicit on requiem but in masquerade is actually the opossite becuase people adicted to the kiss exist and remember the pleasure from the bite triying to replicate it<br /> <br /> <b>Then we get masquerae friendly stuff like this</b><br /> <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/N9stj06/proff.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This is V5 but it also happened similar stuff in revised where in the prologue Alastair informs his childe about how his fellow brujah kills a girl every night he goes to hunt and sees that as a normal thing isntead of a horrible menace to the masquerade that needs to be put under a blood hunt add to this the overpopulation and is easy to see...as the fucks up acumulate <u>the masquerade is unsustainable </u>and this post just constructive crisiticsm signaling an obvious flaw from game design out of love for the universe that i want to see evolve mechanicaly<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 07-02-2020, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T18:57:44-07:00","id":1400609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1400601#post1400601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the feeling that i spoke the truth that everyone knew but also refused to acknowledge with this post and now some people are in negation phase<br /> <br /> The masquerade never was sustainable we just handwaved how things worked becuase we just wanted to tell an story , a lot of us assumed or better said houseruled that the kiss erases the memory something that is explicit on requiem but in masquerade is actually the opossite becuase people adicted to the kiss exist and remember the pleasure from the bite triying to replicate it<br /> <br /> <b>Then we get masquerae friendly stuff like this</b><br /> <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/N9stj06/proff.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This is V5 but it also happened similar stuff in revised where in the prologue Alastair informs his childe about how his fellow brujah kills a girl every night he goes to hunt and sees that as a normal thing isntead of a horrible menace to the masquerade that needs to be put under a blood hunt add to this the overpopulation and is easy to see...as the fucks up acumulate <u>the masquerade is unsustainable </u>and this post just constructive crisiticsm signaling an obvious flaw from game design out of love for the universe that i want to see evolve mechanicaly</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Vampire bite never erased memory in VtM.<br /> <br /> I think it erases in v5, trough.<br /> <br /> Said that, I don't like the idea. Something so CONVENIENT happening to justify to convince me that the masquerade is possible, backfire, ans my suspension of desbelief is damaged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T01:11:43-07:00","id":1400661,"title":"","content":"1- Trusting art is stupid. Art is all about screaming &quot;YO DAWG THIS GAME IS ABOUT VAMPIRES LOOK AT THE COOL SEXY EMPOWERED VAMPIRES&quot; It doesn't represent the masquerade. Imagine if the V5 fashion spreads were representative of what vampires actually wore, or if women in the dark ages smashed people with logs rather than something practical just to prove their strength? Art is dumb shit. <br /> <br /> 2- You sure he's not lying to have you hate this guy? People lie a lot, vampires lie more. <br /> <br /> Your argument is bad and you know it. You look like you're struggling to convince yourself, rather than trying to convince others. The masquerade, at least before vampires were having messy criticals all the time and lost their Auspex/Dominate/Obfuscate abilities, was rock solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:13:51-07:00","id":1400675,"title":"","content":"I let Harry Dresden explain how the Masquerade is SUPPOSED to work to poor Butters:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>\u201cLast year in the U.S. alone more than nine hundred thousand people were reported missing and not found...That's out of three hundred million, total population. That breaks down to about one person in three hundred and twenty-five vanishing. Every year....maybe it's a coincidence, but it's almost the same loss ratio experienced by herd animals on the African savannah to large predators.\u201d</i></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>\u201cTime after time, history demonstrates that when people don't want to believe something, they have enormous skills of ignoring it altogether.\u201d </b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1400661#post1400661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Trusting art is stupid. Art is all about screaming &quot;YO DAWG THIS GAME IS ABOUT VAMPIRES LOOK AT THE COOL SEXY EMPOWERED VAMPIRES&quot; It doesn't represent the masquerade. Imagine if the V5 fashion spreads were representative of what vampires actually wore, or if women in the dark ages smashed people with logs rather than something practical just to prove their strength? Art is dumb shit.<br /> <br /> 2- You sure he's not lying to have you hate this guy? People lie a lot, vampires lie more.<br /> <br /> <b>Your argument is bad and you know it. </b>You look like you're struggling to convince yourself, rather than trying to convince others. The masquerade, at least before vampires were having messy criticals all the time and lost their Auspex/Dominate/Obfuscate abilities, was rock solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not helpful.<br /> <br /> I agree the art doesn't necessarily depict reality, though, at least as defined by the gameline itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-03-2020, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T09:42:28-07:00","id":1400764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1286419-the-masquerade-is-mechanicaly-unsustainable?p=1400609#post1400609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. Vampire bite never erased memory in VtM.<br /> <br /> I think it erases in v5, trough.<br /> <br /> Said that, I don't like the idea. Something so CONVENIENT happening to justify to convince me that the masquerade is possible, backfire, ans my suspension of desbelief is damaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can still fuck up a witness might see you feeding and now you 